From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:42:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: host-common: keep D3cold off for devices that have it
 disabled

Patch 0171 lets the endpoints decide whether the host takes the link
down for system sleep: when every endpoint is in D3hot and can signal
PME from D3cold, the link goes down and PERST# is asserted. A Wi-Fi
chip with Wake-on-WLAN has to stay powered and associated, but the
QCA6390 reports PME from D3cold, so the link went down under it. On
resume MHI found its rings gone, qrtr_mhi failed to prepare its
channels with -22, and the next transfer faulted in mhi_gen_tre: with
Wake-on-WLAN enabled the phone crashed on the first suspend.

Leave the link up for a device that has D3cold turned off, through
pci_dev.no_d3cold or d3cold_allowed in sysfs.
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c
index 5ac2b4dfe9..0c0de5f17a 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pci-host-common.c
@@ -301,6 +301,13 @@ static int __pci_host_common_d3cold_possible(struct pci_dev *pdev,
 	if (pdev->current_state != PCI_D3hot)
 		goto exit;
 
+	/*
+	 * A device that must keep its power, such as a Wi-Fi chip that stays
+	 * associated for Wake-on-WLAN, has D3cold turned off.
+	 */
+	if (pdev->no_d3cold || !pdev->d3cold_allowed)
+		goto exit;
+
 	if (device_may_wakeup(&pdev->dev)) {
 		if (!pci_pme_capable(pdev, PCI_D3cold))
 			goto exit;
